## Article

```catala
declaration scope A:
    input x content integer
    input b content boolean
    output o content integer

scope A:
    definition o equals
    if (if x=0 then false else b) then 0 else 1
```

Note that `-1` is never reached.

```catala-test-cli
$ catala DCalc -s A
let scope A (A_in: A_in): A =
  let get x : integer = A_in.x_in in
  let get b : bool = A_in.b_in in
  let set o : integer =
    error_empty
      ⟨ ⟨true ⊢ ⟨if if x = 0 then false else b then 0 else 1⟩⟩ | false ⊢ ∅ ⟩
  in
  return { A o = o; }
```

```catala-test-cli
$ catala Concolic --conc-optim=incremental -s A
┌─[RESULT]─ Concolic execution ─
│ Executed 3 tests:
│       Inputs │ Outputs
│ ──────── Test #1 ────
│ x_in = 0     │ o = 1
│ b_in = true  │
│ ──────── Test #2 ────
│ x_in = 2     │ o = 0
│ b_in = true  │
│ ──────── Test #3 ────
│ x_in = 2     │ o = 1
│ b_in = false │
└─
```

